          "id": "0a5bb7634135e4dcf1a2c939158dead6d836df1d",
          "message": "Refactor CLI with modular architecture and unified build system (#1)\n\nrefactor(cli): modernize CLI with modular architecture and comprehensive testing\n\n  Complete overhaul of the CLI with a clean, modular architecture:\n\n  **New Architecture:**\n  - Migrated from manual argument parsing to Cobra framework\n  - Separate go.mod in cmd/imx with interface-based design\n  - Modular packages: util, ui, filter, output, processor\n  - Concurrent file processing with worker pools\n\n  **Key Features:**\n  - Comprehensive filtering system (spec, tag, search, pattern)\n  - Multiple output formats (text, json, csv, table, summary)\n  - Auto-select format based on file count (table for single, summary for batch)\n  - Time and GPS formatting options with full support across all formatters\n  - Progress bar support for batch operations\n  - Improved error handling and exit codes\n\n  **Testing & Build:**\n  - Comprehensive test coverage (98.1% for filter, 85.8% for output)\n  - Unified coverage reporting using go workspaces\n  - Updated Makefile for multi-module structure\n  - All targets (lint, fmt, bench, coverage) handle both modules\n\n  **Dependencies:**\n  - github.com/spf13/cobra\n  - github.com/spf13/viper\n  - github.com/fatih/color\n  - github.com/schollz/progressbar/v3\n\n  Maintains full backward compatibility with existing features.\n\n  🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n  This simplified version:\n  - Combines all the incremental changes into one cohesive message\n  - Groups related changes under clear sections\n  - Removes redundant information about individual fixes\n  - Keeps the important technical details and architecture decisions\n  - Maintains the co-authorship attribution",
